; Drive build, HDDSYNTH.INI `isa = on`: releases IORDY when ide_bus has held
; it low for about 23 us with no strobe. ISA IDE cards select the drive from
; the address alone, so a memory cycle or DRAM refresh whose address aliases
; 1F0h-1F7h selects it too, and pass IORDY to IOCHRDY: ide_bus pulls IORDY low
; at the chip select (as ATA's timing needs) and, with no strobe to end the
; access, the cycle would stall for good (an ICL 386 froze, 0.21.0). The
; longest gap the ICL's BIOS left between a status read and its data, with
; the drive still selected, was 11 us. Once released, IORDY stays released
; until ide_bus pulls it low again (its next `arm` or `read`): a stalled
; cycle ends however slowly the host's pull-up raises the line, which a 60 ns
; release (0.21.2) didn't allow.
;
; The count starts over whenever IORDY reads high or a strobe (DIOR# or
; DIOW#) is asserted: a strobe means a real access, which core 1 answers.
; Up to 0.32.1-dev.5 only IORDY high started it over, and between back-to-back
; data reads IORDY is high at the pin for only a moment (ide_bus pulls it low
; again about 25 ns after DIOR# rises, before the host's pull-up has raised
; it far). Missing those moments for 23 us, the watchdog took a run of reads
; for one hold and released IORDY mid-read: the Evesham read about one data
; word in 2.5 million before the drive drove it (docs/atapi.md). A strobe
; lasts at least 70 ns (t2, PIO mode 4) and this loop looks every 30 ns.
;
; Runs in ide_bus's PIO block (ide_bus.cpp), whose 32 instructions the two
; fill (23 + 9), so both write the same pin direction register: this program only ever writes 0 (release). DIOR# skips
; the input synchroniser there; a level is all this program needs of it.
;
; Pin mapping:
;   IN_BASE  = GPIO4 (DD0), as in bus_sample.h: DIOR# is bit 22, DIOW# bit 23
;   JMP_PIN  = GPIO28 (IORDY): high once released, by either program
;   SET      = GPIO28, as a pin direction
;   wait 0 gpio 28: ide_bus has pulled it low
; ISR holds the count, passes - 1, put there before the program starts (it
; never shifts in); a pass is 6 cycles: 767 passes, 23 us at 200 MHz
; (host/tests/test_iordy_watchdog_sim.py).

.pio_version 1
.program iordy_watchdog
.wrap_target
top:
    wait 0 gpio 28                  ; ide_bus has pulled IORDY low
    mov y, isr                      ; the count
hold:
    jmp pin top                     ; released meanwhile: start over
    mov osr, ~pins                  ; sample, inverted (asserted = 1)
    out null, 22                    ; drop DD0-15, DA0-2, CS0#, CS1#, LED
    out x, 2                        ; DIOR#, DIOW#
    jmp x-- top                     ; a strobe: a real access, start over
    jmp y-- hold
    set pindirs, 0                  ; held too long: release it
.wrap
